diff --git a/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEAS.md b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEAS.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..dcc69047
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEAS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# CVE-2026-53615 — Already Fixed in Debian Trixie util-linux 2.41.5-0+deb13u1
+
+## Summary
+
+**CVE-2026-53615 is already fixed in the util-linux package this hook targets.**
+The uint32_t overflow in `libblkid` `parse_dos_extended()` is present in trixie
+`2.41-5`, but **Debian security `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` already contains the upstream
+EBR bounds-check / 64-bit arithmetic fix**. Re-applying the upstream patch fails
+as reversed or already applied. This file is documentation only.
+
+---
+
+## CVE Description
+
+> A uint32_t integer overflow in `parse_dos_extended()` at
+> `libblkid/src/partitions/dos.c` allows a crafted disk image to make libblkid
+> register a partition at sector 0 (the MBR). The addition
+> `abs_start = cur_start + start` lacked an overflow guard for EBR loop entries
+> `i=0` and `i=1`. Downstream tools (udisks2, blkid, mkfs) can then treat the
+> wrapped value as a valid partition covering the MBR.
+
+- **CVE ID:** CVE-2026-53615
+- **Advisory:** [GHSA-h4rw-gv36-wmp5](https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-h4rw-gv36-wmp5)
+- **Upstream fix commits:**
+  - `e9d544d013267ea86b70ee8ff78abd280e6641af` (orig)
+  - `05c2dbadf34cc74192287f377904afaaf4061623` (v2.41.4)
+- **Debian security tracker:** https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615
+  (trixie security `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` = **fixed**)
+
+---
+
+## Affected Package in Debian Trixie
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Package | util-linux |
+| Trixie main | `2.41-5` (vulnerable) |
+| Trixie security (this hook) | `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` (**fixed**) |
+| Upstream base | util-linux v2.41.5 |
+
+---
+
+## Why No Code Patch Is Applied Here
+
+### 1. Debian already shipped the fix
+
+The Debian tracker marks trixie security `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` as fixed. The orig
+tarball for 2.41.5 includes the v2.41.4 `dos.c` change (`ex_end` / 64-bit
+arithmetic).
+
+### 2. Direct code verification
+
+`libblkid/src/partitions/dos.c` in `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` already contains the
+overflow-safe EBR handling. Applying
+`e9d544d013267ea86b70ee8ff78abd280e6641af` / `05c2dbadf34cc74192287f377904afaaf4061623`
+again is rejected as already applied.
+
+### 3. This is not a "never affected" false positive
+
+Trixie `2.41-5` **was** vulnerable. This hook's `applicable_version` is the
+already-fixed security package, so a dummy documentation patch is used instead
+of a second code backport.
+
+---
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Date | Event |
+|---|---|
+| 2026 | CVE-2026-53615; orig fix `e9d544d0` |
+| 2026 | v2.41.4 backport `05c2dbadf3` |
+| 2026 | Debian trixie security `2.41.5-0+deb13u1` marked fixed |
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+**Do not re-apply a code patch for CVE-2026-53615 on `2.41.5-0+deb13u1`.**
+Treat scanner hits against this exact version as already remediated by Debian.
+Hits against trixie `2.41-5` are real and are out of scope for this hook.
+
+---
+
+## References
+
+- Orig fix: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/e9d544d013267ea86b70ee8ff78abd280e6641af
+- v2.41.4 fix: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/commit/05c2dbadf34cc74192287f377904afaaf4061623
+- GitHub advisory: https://github.com/util-linux/util-linux/security/advisories/GHSA-h4rw-gv36-wmp5
+- Debian security tracker: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615
